# Project Structure Guide

This is an Astro-based personal website/portfolio project. Here's how the project is organized:

## Core Configuration
- [astro.config.mjs](mdc:astro.config.mjs) - Main Astro configuration
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Project dependencies and scripts

## Source Code Organization
The main source code is in the `src` directory:
- `src/pages/` - Astro pages and routes
- `src/components/` - Reusable UI components
- `src/layouts/` - Page layouts and templates
- `src/styles/` - Global styles and CSS
- `src/utils/` - Utility functions and helpers
- `src/images/` - Image assets
- [src/content.config.ts](mdc:src/content.config.ts) - Content collection configuration

## Content
Content is organized in two main directories:
- `content/blog/` - Blog posts and articles
- `content/work-experience/` - Work experience entries

## Public Assets
Static assets are stored in the `public/` directory and are served directly.
